# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://www.yomama-jokes.com/docs/"
      }
      description: "API for retrieving jokes by random, category, or list based on Yo Mama jokes. No authentication required."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://api.yomomma.info"
        }
      ]
      title: "Yo Mama API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Fetch random Yo Mama jokes as JSON, with optional category filtering"
      homepage: "https://api.yomomma.info"
      docs_url: "https://freepublicapis.com/yo-mama-api"
      license_short: "No licence terms published; free public endpoint"
      license_md: `- No licence or terms of use are published for the joke corpus
- No authentication or API key is required
- No attribution requirements are documented
- CORS is reportedly disabled, so browser-side calls may need a proxy`
      about_md: `The [Yo Mama API](https://api.yomomma.info) is a small free service that returns Yo Mama jokes as JSON. There is no published maintainer information or formal documentation; the most useful third-party reference is the [Free Public APIs catalogue page](https://freepublicapis.com/yo-mama-api).

What you get from the API:

- A random Yo Mama joke from the full corpus
- A random joke restricted to a specific category (e.g. \`fat\`)
- A listing of jokes grouped by category

No API key, OAuth, or sign-up is required. Rate limits are not documented. CORS is reported as disabled on all endpoints, so client-side use from a browser may require a server-side proxy.`
      entity_desc: {
        category: "A named grouping of Yo Mama jokes (for example `fat`) used to scope listing and random-joke requests."
        get_random_joke: "Operation that returns a single randomly selected joke from the corpus via `GET /api/random`."
        joke: "A single Yo Mama joke resource returned as JSON, either at random or as part of a category listing."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
